# Deploy Conventions

## Docker Compose Services

| Service | Image / build | Host ports | Depends on |
|---------|----------------|------------|------------|
| mysql | mysql:8.0 | 3307 | — |
| openfga-migrate | alpine:3.19 | — | mysql |
| openfga | openfga/openfga:v1.5.3 | 8180, 8181, 3001 | mysql, openfga-migrate |
| openfga-init | alpine:3.19 | — | openfga |
| clickhouse | clickhouse/clickhouse-server:25.4 | 8123, 9000 | — |
| kafka | confluentinc/cp-kafka:7.6.0 | 9092 | — |
| minio | minio/minio:latest | 9100→9000, 9101→9001 (console) | — |
| minio-init | minio/mc:latest | — | minio |
| clickhouse-init | clickhouse/clickhouse-server:25.4 | — | clickhouse **and** kafka (healthy) |
| pulse-session-capture | `backend/session-capture-service` | 3400 | kafka |
| pulse-session-replay-ingestion | `backend/session-replay-ingestion` | — | kafka, minio-init |
| pulse-heatmap-screenshot-ingestion | `backend/heatmap-screenshot-ingestion` | — | kafka, minio-init |
| pulse-s3-archiver | `backend/pulse-s3-archiver/` | — (compose health: in-container `:5000/healthcheck`) | kafka (healthy) |
| otel-collector | otel-collector-contrib:0.137.0 | 4317, 4318, 8888, 13133 | clickhouse |
| vector | `650012445044.../pulse-vector:latest` | 8686, 14317, 14318 | — | *(profile `vector`; `VECTOR_ENABLED=true`)* |
| pulse-ai-agent | `pulse_ai/` | 8000 | — |
| pulse-server | `backend/server/` | 8080 | mysql, clickhouse, openfga-init, pulse-ai-agent |
| pulse-ui | `pulse-ui/` | 3000 | pulse-server |
| pulse-alerts-cron | `backend/pulse-alerts-cron/` | 4000 | mysql, pulse-server, minio-init |

**pulse-s3-archiver:** Kafka OTLP protobuf topics (`pulse.traces` / `pulse.logs` / `pulse.metrics`) → Parquet → **one S3 bucket per project** (`pulse-otel-{sanitized project.id}` from resource `project.id`; missing id → `pulse-otel-unknown`). No single **`S3_BUCKET`** env — provision buckets / IAM (**`s3:PutObject`**) accordingly. Compose passes **`S3_REGION`**, optional **`S3_ENDPOINT`** (MinIO in stack: internal `http://minio:9000` if you expose it via network), **`AWS_*`**, **`ARCHIVER_FLUSH_INTERVAL_MS`**, **`ARCHIVER_STAGING_DIR`**, optional **`PULSE_BACKEND_OTEL_ENABLED`**. Healthcheck in compose targets `:5000` inside the container; **host port not published** by default.

**otel-collector:** healthcheck is disabled in compose (scratch image); use `:13133` from the host for health.

**clickhouse-init:** mounts `backend/db/dev/clickhouse/*.sql`, session replay + session-summary MV, `event-catalog-entries.sql`, `funnel-results.sql`, `journey-results.sql`; runs `deploy/scripts/init-clickhouse.sh` (applies otel, session replay, session-summary MV, and funnel/journey schemas when present).

`pulse-server` and `pulse-alerts-cron` include `extra_hosts: host.docker.internal:host-gateway` so containers can reach OTLP on the host (optional JVM OpenTelemetry export; see below).

## Optional observability stack (Prometheus + Tempo + Grafana)

Not started by the main Pulse compose. Separate project: `deploy/observability-otel-prometheus-tempo/` (see `README.md` there). Typical start: `cd deploy/observability-otel-prometheus-tempo && docker compose up -d`.

- **Services:** MinIO, `minio-init`, Tempo, **`obs_otel_collector`** (name avoids clashing with deploy stack `otel-collector`), Prometheus, Grafana. Prometheus loads **`prometheus/rules/pulse-otel.yml`** recording rules (RED-style `otel:http_server:*` metrics) for use in the Prometheus **Graph** UI.
- **Host ports (avoid clashes with main stack):** OTLP **14317/14318**, Grafana **3310**, Prometheus **9091**, MinIO **9002/9003**, Tempo **3200**, collector self-metrics **18889** (Prometheus scrape), collector health **13134** → 13133 in-container.

**Port conflict:** Host OTLP **14317/14318** match the optional **Vector** profile in `deploy/docker-compose.yml`. Do not run Vector and this observability stack on the same machine without changing one compose’s published ports.

**JVM telemetry from Pulse backends:** Set `PULSE_BACKEND_OTEL_ENABLED=true` in `deploy/.env` and **rebuild** `pulse-server` / `pulse-alerts-cron` images so the OpenTelemetry Java agent is present. Entrypoint defaults OTLP to `http://host.docker.internal:14318` when the observability stack listens on the host. Use `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` / `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` to override.

**Pulse AI:** `pulse-ai-agent` is part of the default deploy stack (`docker compose up`). Set `GOOGLE_API_KEY` in `deploy/.env` for Gemini; the process starts without it but model/API calls fail. **Standalone** AI-only dev: `pulse_ai/docker-compose.yml` + `cd pulse_ai && ./setup.sh [start|stop|restart|logs|clean]`.

## Network

All services on `pulse-network` (bridge). Internal references use container names (e.g., `mysql`, `clickhouse:8123`, `openfga:8080`).

## Volumes

`mysql-data`, `clickhouse-data`, `kafka-data`, `minio-data` — persistent. Use `./scripts/reset-databases.sh` to wipe. (`vector-data` when Vector profile is enabled.) `pulse-ai-sessions` — SQLite session store for integrated `pulse-ai-agent` (not removed by `reset-databases.sh`; remove volume manually if needed).

## Environment Variables

- `APP_ENVIRONMENT` — **Required.** Application environment (`dev`, `stag`, `uat`, `prod`). Validated at startup. Passed to pulse-server in docker-compose (default: `dev`).
- `CONFIG_SERVICE_APPLICATION_*` — backend app config
- `CONFIG_SERVICE_APPLICATION_DASHBOARDBASEURL` — Public Pulse UI origin for usage-limit email links (`pulse-server` HOCON `app.dashboardBaseUrl`; compose default `http://localhost:3000` on `pulse-server` in `deploy/docker-compose.yml`).
- `CONFIG_REPLAY_API_BASE_URL` — session replay API base URL (e.g. `http://localhost:3400`); used in default SDK config
- `VAULT_SERVICE_*` — secrets (Slack, Grafana, etc.)
- `OTEL_CLICKHOUSE_*` — OTEL collector ClickHouse connection
- `REACT_APP_*` — frontend build-time config
- `NOTIFICATION_*` — notification service (SQS queue URLs, retry, worker tuning)
- `SES_*` — Amazon SES email config
- `SLACK_*` — Slack OAuth integration (client ID, secret, scopes, redirect URI, UI redirect URL)
- `OPENFGA_*` — OpenFGA authorization service config
- `AWS_*` — AWS credentials for Athena/S3 (also **`pulse-s3-archiver`** `PutObject` into per-project `pulse-otel-*` buckets; MinIO compose uses **`MINIO_ROOT_*`** IAM-style keys unless overridden)
- `COMPOSE_PROFILES` — Optional. Used for Vector (`VECTOR_ENABLED=true` appends `vector`). Plain `docker compose` also reads this env when set manually.
- `GOOGLE_API_KEY` — Google GenAI / ADK for `pulse-ai-agent` (process starts without it; Gemini calls fail at runtime).
- `PULSE_BASE_URL` — Base URL for pulse_ai tools → pulse-server (compose default: `http://pulse-server:8080`).
- `SESSION_DB_URL` — AI session DB; compose defaults to SQLite on volume `pulse-ai-sessions`.
- `AI_SERVICE_URL` — URL pulse-server uses for AI proxy (compose default: `http://pulse-ai-agent:8000`). Override (e.g. `http://host.docker.internal:8000`) when AI runs on the host or outside deploy compose.
- `SPAN_COLLECTOR_URL` — OTLP span collector endpoint (default: `http://localhost:4318/v1/traces`)
- `LOGS_COLLECTOR_URL` — OTLP logs collector endpoint (default: `http://localhost:4318/v1/logs`)
- `METRIC_COLLECTOR_URL` — OTLP metrics collector endpoint (default: `http://localhost:4318/v1/metrics`)
- `CUSTOM_EVENT_COLLECTOR_URL` — Custom event collector endpoint (default: `http://localhost:4318/v1/logs`)
- `INTERACTION_CONFIG_URL` — Interaction config for pulse-server (project flows); in compose, passed through from `.env` (see `deploy/.env.example` — e.g. `http://pulse-server:8080/v1/interaction-configs/` in-stack, or host/dev URLs). **Not** the OTLP traces URL.
- `VECTOR_ENABLED` — Optional. Set to `true` when using Vector (custom events → S3/Athena). The Vector **service is commented out** in `docker-compose.yml` until you uncomment it. Default: `false`.
- `REDIS_URL` / `REDIS_HOST` + `REDIS_PORT` — Optional; used by `pulse-heatmap-screenshot-ingestion` when pointing at an **external** Redis (not a compose service here). Empty `REDIS_URL` and `REDIS_HOST` disables Redis-backed quota/dedupe in that worker. Compose also passes **`REDIS_HOST`** / **`REDIS_PORT`** to **`pulse-server`** for Kong plugin materialization (API key map + usage credits in Redis); `pulse-alerts-cron` triggers internal POSTs on pulse-server—cron does **not** connect to Redis or ClickHouse directly.
- `HEATMAP_QUOTA_PER_DAY`, `HEATMAP_QUOTA_TTL_SECONDS`, `HEATMAP_DEDUPE_TTL_SECONDS` — Optional; heatmap ingestion quota/dedupe TTLs (defaults in compose; see `deploy/.env.example`).
- `HEATMAP_S3_BUCKET`, `HEATMAP_S3_ENDPOINT`, `HEATMAP_S3_PRESIGN_ENDPOINT`, `HEATMAP_S3_REGION`, `HEATMAP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `HEATMAP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` — Heatmap screenshot **dedicated** bucket (`heatmap-assets` by default). **`HEATMAP_S3_ENDPOINT`** is for listing (e.g. `http://minio:9000` in compose). **`HEATMAP_S3_PRESIGN_ENDPOINT`** (pulse-server only): browser-facing host for presigned URLs; local example `http://localhost:9100` (MinIO on host is **9100**; host **9000** is ClickHouse). Omit in AWS if default S3 URLs are fine. Omitted endpoint/keys fall back to session replay MinIO settings. Unset `HEATMAP_S3_BUCKET` → pulse-server uses `SESSION_REPLAY_S3_BUCKET` for heatmap keys (legacy).
- `HEATMAP_SCREENSHOTS_S3_PREFIX` — Optional; S3 object key prefix (default `heatmap-screenshots`).
- `MINIO_ROOT_USER` / `MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD` — MinIO dev credentials (compose defaults: `pulse_minio` / `pulse_minio_secret`).
- `SESSION_REPLAY_*` — S3-style endpoint/bucket/keys for session recordings (pulse-server; in compose defaults to MinIO on `minio:9000`).
- `ROOT_CAUSE_ENABLED` — Backend root-cause API (pulse-server).
- `REACT_APP_ROOT_CAUSE_ENABLED` — UI build arg for RCA tab (must align with backend when enabling).
- `CONFIG_SERVICE_APPLICATION_SPARK_JOB_*` — Spark batch entry classes in compose default to `org.dreamhorizon.pulsespark.SparkJobRunner` for funnels, journeys, and events (override via `.env` if needed).
- `ANALYTICS_COMPUTE_ENGINE` — Product analytics batch routing: `spark` (EMR) vs `clickhouse` (in-process). Mapped from `backend/server/src/main/resources/conf/analytics-engine-default.conf`. Docker Compose default: `clickhouse` (see `deploy/docker-compose.yml`); `deploy/scripts/common.sh` `load_env` defaults to `spark` for CLI `start.sh` when unset.
- `ANALYTICS_BATCH_PROJECT_CONCURRENCY` — Max concurrent per-project ClickHouse batch queries when engine is `clickhouse`; required **> 0** in `prod` (`StartupConfigValidator`). Compose default: `1`; `load_env` default: `4`.
- `CONFIG_SERVICE_APPLICATION_INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKENS` — Comma-separated opaque bearer tokens for internal service authentication (pulse-alerts-cron).

**Dev Mode Configuration:**
- `GOOGLE_OAUTH_ENABLED` — Enable/disable Google OAuth login (default: `false` for dev mode)
- `DEV_MODE_API_KEY` — Hardcoded API key for default-project when OAuth is disabled (default: `default-project_devkey01`). Format: `{projectId}_{suffix}` (single underscore for project ID extraction).

Credentials (defined in docker-compose, overridable via `.env`):
- MySQL: `MYSQL_USER` / `MYSQL_PASSWORD` (defaults: `pulse_user` / `pulse_password`)
- ClickHouse: `OTEL_CLICKHOUSE_USER` / `OTEL_CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD` (defaults: `pulse_user` / `pulse_password`)
- ClickHouse Cluster: `CLICKHOUSE_CLUSTER_NAME` — Passed to pulse-server in docker-compose. Use empty string for single-node (local dev). Must be non-blank in `prod`.
- OpenFGA: `OPENFGA_STORE_ID` / `OPENFGA_MODEL_ID` (generated by init script)

**pulse-server → ClickHouse in Compose:** `CLICKHOUSE_R2DBC_URL` is set to `r2dbc:clickhouse:http://clickhouse:8123/${OTEL_CLICKHOUSE_DATABASE:-otel}` (service name `clickhouse`, not overridden by `CLICKHOUSE_HOST` in `.env`). `CLICKHOUSE_HOST` and `CLICKHOUSE_PORT` in the pulse-server service are literals (`clickhouse`, `8123`). `CLICKHOUSE_USERNAME` / `CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD` for the JVM config come from **`OTEL_CLICKHOUSE_USER`** / **`OTEL_CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD`**, not from bare `CLICKHOUSE_USERNAME` unless you map them in compose. To point pulse-server at an external ClickHouse replica, change `deploy/docker-compose.yml` (or a profile override) to substitute host/URL and ensure the container can resolve and reach that host.

## Scripts

| Script | Options |
|--------|---------|
| `build.sh` | `[--no-cache]` and targets `ui`, `server`, `cron`, `capture`, `ingestion`, `heatmap` \| `heatmap-ingestion`, `s3-archiver` \| `pulse-s3-archiver`, `ai`, `all` — default (no args) or `all` builds UI, server, cron, capture, session replay ingestion, **heatmap screenshot ingestion**, **pulse-s3-archiver**, and AI (`capture` = pulse-session-capture; `ingestion` = pulse-session-replay-ingestion; `heatmap-ingestion` = pulse-heatmap-screenshot-ingestion; **`s3-archiver`** = `pulse-s3-archiver`) |
| `start.sh` | `[-d` or `--detach] [--build] [--no-cache] [--skip-env-check]` |
| `stop.sh` | `-v` to remove volumes; service aliases include `ai`, `pulse-ai-agent` |
| `logs.sh` | service name (e.g., `server`, `ai`, `otel-collector`) |
| `quickstart.sh` | `[--no-cache] [--skip-env-check]` — builds + starts stack (includes AI) |
| `reset-databases.sh` | drops volumes and reinitializes |
| `init-clickhouse.sh` | creates ClickHouse tables from schema SQL + session-summary MV; optional funnel/journey SQL when files are present |

**Env validation:** `quickstart.sh` and `start.sh` validate `.env` against `docker-compose.yml`: **required** = variables in compose with no default (`${VAR}`); missing in `.env` → error. **Optional** = variables with a default in compose (`${VAR:-...}`); missing in `.env` → warning (compose uses default). No auto-copy from `.env.example`; only required keys must be set. Collector/config URL vars must be valid `http://` or `https://` URLs. Use `--skip-env-check` to skip. The parser in `deploy/scripts/common.sh` retains the last line even when `.env` has no trailing newline (e.g. pasted tokens).

**Required (no default in compose):** `VAULT_ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY`, `REACT_APP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `REACT_APP_FIREBASE_*`, `CONFIG_SERVICE_APPLICATION_GOOGLEOAUTHCLIENTID`, `CONFIG_SERVICE_APPLICATION_GCP_PROJECT_ID`, `CONFIG_SERVICE_APPLICATION_WEBHOOKURL`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` / `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN`. Must be set in `.env`. `SLACK_*` are optional (default empty; needed only for Slack API integration).


**Cursor config audit:** Service list and env rules match `deploy/docker-compose.yml`. Vector is optional: uncomment its service in compose and set `VECTOR_ENABLED=true` in `.env`. `pulse-server` `depends_on` `pulse-ai-agent` with `condition: service_healthy`. Heatmap ingestion uses external Redis via `REDIS_*` and optional `HEATMAP_*` as above. **`pulse-alerts-cron`** compose env is MySQL + `CONFIG_SERVICE_APPLICATION_*` only (no per-cron ClickHouse/Redis vars); it does not `depends_on` ClickHouse.

